 kit issues - lists the forge's milestones and iterations of the repository

   one of
   *kit issues*  lists the forge's milestones and iterations of the repository

     --text   --json   --jq
                           prints the stages as text, even on a terminal

   --stages    prints the stages, one per line, in order, the same over any workspace
   --marks     prints a mark per stage, as one JSON object, which changes when what the stage draws
               does: the forge's own mark of its milestones for milestones, null for iterations,
               which has none
   milestones  {number, title, state, due, open, closed}: state is open or closed, due is seconds
               since the epoch or null for none, open and closed count the milestone's issues; the
               title links to its page. Azure DevOps has no milestones
   iterations  {id, title, start, end, current}: start and end are seconds since the epoch, end the
               last second of the last day, null where the iteration has no dates; current is true
               for the one that holds now; the title links to the page of the project, the
               iteration, or the team's sprints. A repository with no project linked on GitHub has
               none
   backlog     a tab kit flow prints; on a terminal it opens in kittui, and with a form it is
               refused
   underway    a tab kit flow prints; on a terminal it opens in kittui, and with a form it is
               refused


 kit issues
